{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), the most critical uncertainty is the relative contribution of each modality. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-factor ablation that isolates the image modality's standalone signal while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) and architectural simplicity (no aggregation/fusion) matched to config_001. This establishes the image baseline needed to interpret all future multimodal experiments: if image_only substantially outperforms rna_only, the image modality is the stronger signal source and multimodal fusion should be prioritized; if it underperforms, RNA-focused improvements (better encoders, multiprofile) become more valuable. Testing multimodal directly (e.g., config_016) would confound the image contribution with fusion strategy, reducing interpretability. Under a tight budget, this one experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis (modality) before committing to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

